      "sequence_position": 2,
      "problem": "If $f(x)=x-7$ and $g(x)=2{x}^{2}-4$, then $(fg)(x)=$",
      "worked_solution": "The notation $(fg)(x)$ means the product of the functions $f(x)$ and $g(x).$\n\nTo find the product of the two functions, we multiply them together: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(fg)(x) & =f(x)g(x) \\\\  & =(x-7)(2{x}^{2}-4) \\\\  & =2{x}^{3}-4x-14{x}^{2}+28 \\\\  & =2{x}^{3}-14{x}^{2}-4x+28\\end{aligned}\n$$",
